    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25856" root="ضعف" body-key="D">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَضْعُوفٌ</span></b> , applied to a thing, (S,) or to a man,
(O,) <i>Rendered</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَعِيف</span> [i. e. <i>weak,</i> &amp;c.]: (AA, S,
O, K:) by rule it should be <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُضْعَفٌ</span>. (O, K.) A
man <i>weak in intellect:</i> (IAar, TA:) or <i>weakhearted and having little intellect.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See
also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْضٌ مُضَعَّفَةٌ</span>, above.

